WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.567 --> 00:00:03.601
-Welcome back to the show.
I always love having you on.

00:00:03.601 --> 00:00:04.634
-Thank you for having me on.

00:00:04.634 --> 00:00:06.100
-Well, thank you
for being nice to us

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:09.133
when we were Zooming the show
and we really needed guests.

00:00:09.133 --> 00:00:10.567
So thank you so much.
I appreciate it.

00:00:10.567 --> 00:00:13.334
-It's my pleasure.
It's back to business now.

00:00:13.334 --> 00:00:15.234
-How are the kids doing?
-They're good.

00:00:15.234 --> 00:00:17.367
It's a lot of Halloween fever
in my house.

00:00:17.367 --> 00:00:20.767
-6 and --
-Yes, they're 6 and 5.

00:00:20.767 --> 00:00:22.634
-Yeah. And so Halloween fever.
What are they being?

00:00:22.634 --> 00:00:24.100
-Yes. It's hectic.

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:27.300
So, Rocco, my 6-year-old --
he decides he's in charge,

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:28.734
so I'm Wonder Woman.

00:00:28.734 --> 00:00:32.734
-Ah, there you go. Good.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:00:32.734 --> 00:00:34.234
I just got my costume
in the mail.

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:35.734
It's pretty nasty.

00:00:35.734 --> 00:00:37.267
-You got to fix it.

00:00:37.267 --> 00:00:40.534
-Yeah, I got to do
a little customizing.

00:00:40.534 --> 00:00:42.567
And Bobby's
going to be The Hulk.

00:00:42.567 --> 00:00:44.567
-Oh, of course.

00:00:44.567 --> 00:00:47.501
-Yep.
And Rocco's going to be Thor.

00:00:47.501 --> 00:00:51.234
And my little one, Rafa --
he's going to be Jafar.

00:00:51.234 --> 00:00:55.167
-Wow! Interesting.
Interesting curveball.

00:00:55.167 --> 00:00:56.634
He's like,
"No, I want to be Jafar."

00:00:56.634 --> 00:00:59.400
-Yeah, he was practicing
his voice last night.

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:01.667
You know, "The rest of
the treasure is mine!"

00:01:01.667 --> 00:01:03.033
Like that.

00:01:03.033 --> 00:01:05.767
-"Just give him the treat,
and he'll get off your lawn.

00:01:05.767 --> 00:01:07.501
Sorry. We'll get it right
for Halloween."

00:01:07.501 --> 00:01:11.067
-You know, the little hat on.
-Yeah, it's so cute.

00:01:11.067 --> 00:01:12.901
In Australia,
did you have Halloween?

00:01:12.901 --> 00:01:14.300
Was it a big thing?
-No, we didn't.

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:17.133
It was like, you know,
we had, like, a crappy pair of,

00:01:17.133 --> 00:01:20.234
like, cardboard ears
and drew on, you know, whiskers.

00:01:20.234 --> 00:01:22.067
And, like, you'd knock on doors
and get, like,

00:01:22.067 --> 00:01:23.968
you know, a carrot and an apple.

00:01:23.968 --> 00:01:25.400
Something. They're like,
"What are you doing here?"

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:27.534
-Wow! Yeah.
Wonder why it didn't take off.

00:01:27.534 --> 00:01:29.834
-I know, I know.
It wasn't really a thing.

00:01:29.834 --> 00:01:33.067
But here, it's like magic.
I'm so into it.

00:01:33.067 --> 00:01:34.400
-Oh, it's the greatest thing.
-It's wonderful.

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:36.234
-Well, last time Bobby was here,

00:01:36.234 --> 00:01:37.834
he was telling me
about this movie --

00:01:37.834 --> 00:01:39.534
he's playing
a Neil Diamond impersonator --

00:01:39.534 --> 00:01:41.200
that you're producing?

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:42.901
-Yes, I produce with my company,
Dollhouse Pictures.

00:01:42.901 --> 00:01:44.000
It's called "Seriously Red."

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:45.801
And he kindly did
a little cameo --

00:01:45.801 --> 00:01:46.868
Well, he has a big part in it,

00:01:46.868 --> 00:01:48.300
and I do
a little cameo, as well, yes.

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:50.367
-Yeah, you play
an Elvis impersonator.

00:01:50.367 --> 00:01:52.334
-Yes, it's set in the world of
impersonators, obviously.

00:01:52.334 --> 00:01:54.801
-Here's you as --
The debut of you as Elvis.

00:01:54.801 --> 00:01:57.400
-Yes.
-Yeah, not bad.

00:01:57.400 --> 00:01:58.868
I like this.

00:01:58.868 --> 00:02:00.701
Did you --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:00.701 --> 00:02:03.267
Did you have
an Elvis impersonation?

00:02:03.267 --> 00:02:04.801
-I mean, yeah.

00:02:04.801 --> 00:02:07.501
It's like, you know, "Thank you
very much," that kind of thing.

00:02:07.501 --> 00:02:09.868
But it's not --
You know, "impersonator"

00:02:09.868 --> 00:02:11.400
is the key,
but it was a lot of fun.

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:14.100
We shot during COVID in 2020.
And it's --

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:15.334
-What made you think, "Elvis --

00:02:15.334 --> 00:02:16.634
that's the one I'm going to do"?

00:02:16.634 --> 00:02:18.501
-Well, my girlfriend, Krew --
she wrote the story.

00:02:18.501 --> 00:02:20.067
And it's about a young woman
called Raylene,

00:02:20.067 --> 00:02:22.200
who's a bit of a misfit,
and her aspiration in life

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:24.033
is to be a
Dolly Parton impersonator.

00:02:24.033 --> 00:02:26.234
So it's an ode to Dolly Parton.

00:02:26.234 --> 00:02:28.434
It's a love letter to her,
about her music,

00:02:28.434 --> 00:02:30.934
and the icon she is.

00:02:30.934 --> 00:02:32.801
-And the characters you meet
and the people you meet.

00:02:32.801 --> 00:02:34.434
-Yes, yes.
-Are you so excited?

00:02:34.434 --> 00:02:36.868
You are a global ambassador
of Australia.

00:02:36.868 --> 00:02:40.267
-I know.
-Rose, it doesn't get bigger.

00:02:40.267 --> 00:02:42.200
[ Cheers and applause ]
It doesn't get bigger.

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:45.434
"Come and Say G'day."
Rose Byrne, you've done it all.

00:02:45.434 --> 00:02:49.467
-Come and say g'day, mate.
Yeah, it's so surreal.

00:02:49.467 --> 00:02:51.234
These campaigns have
a great legacy in Australia.

00:02:51.234 --> 00:02:54.000
And, you know,
Paul Hogan famously did one

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:55.334
and Chris Hemsworth
and Kylie Minogue.

00:02:55.334 --> 00:02:58.634
So I feel very honored to
be part of this kind of story.

00:02:58.634 --> 00:02:59.634
And, yeah, it's incredible.

00:02:59.634 --> 00:03:02.200
-Are your parents excited?

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:03.501
-They are excited.

00:03:03.501 --> 00:03:06.501
I took my dad -- We shot some of
the campaign in Uluru,

00:03:06.501 --> 00:03:08.133
which is in
the middle of Australia.

00:03:08.133 --> 00:03:09.434
It's an incredible spot.

00:03:09.434 --> 00:03:11.400
And I took my dad,
which was really cute.

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:13.133
My parents
are here tonight backstage.

00:03:13.133 --> 00:03:14.234
What's up, Mom and Dad?

00:03:14.234 --> 00:03:15.434
-I did get a chance
to say hi to them.

00:03:15.434 --> 00:03:17.033
-I know.
-They're so cute.

00:03:17.033 --> 00:03:18.968
-My brother is here.
-And your brother, too, yeah.

00:03:18.968 --> 00:03:21.167
-He thinks I should retire
now I got this campaign.

00:03:21.167 --> 00:03:22.601
-Yeah, of course.
He's like, "Oh, really?

00:03:22.601 --> 00:03:24.601
What else could
happen to you, Rose?

00:03:24.601 --> 00:03:26.100
Oh, my gosh.
The favorite child."

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:27.667
Yeah.
-No, no, no.

00:03:27.667 --> 00:03:29.300
-What's your brother's name?
-George.

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:32.501
-Do they -- Everyone
has nicknames in Australia.

00:03:32.501 --> 00:03:33.901
-Yes, we do. We do, yeah.

00:03:33.901 --> 00:03:35.767
-Georgie?
-Jerry.

00:03:35.767 --> 00:03:37.968
-They call him Jerry?
-Yeah, Jerry. Jerry Dog.

00:03:37.968 --> 00:03:41.100
-Jerry Dog, yeah.
What would I be called?

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:42.934
-Well, 'cause you're --
You're James obviously, right?

00:03:42.934 --> 00:03:46.234
-Yeah, James, yeah.
-So Jim, so Jimbo.

00:03:46.234 --> 00:03:50.033
-I've been called Jimbo.
-Jimmy Jimmy Jimmy Jack.

00:03:50.033 --> 00:03:51.834
-I like Jimmy Jimmy Jimmy Jack.

00:03:51.834 --> 00:03:53.767
Yeah, that's pretty fun.

00:03:53.767 --> 00:03:55.968
Well, the big part of the
campaign -- Here you are here.

00:03:55.968 --> 00:03:58.234
You are Ruby.
-Yes. Ruby the Roo.

00:03:58.234 --> 00:04:01.968
-You are the toy souvenir
of, yeah, a kangaroo.

00:04:01.968 --> 00:04:05.300
This is --
And also the director.

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:07.834
-Yes. He's an old friend of
mine, Michael Gracey,

00:04:07.834 --> 00:04:09.901
who directed
"The Greatest Showman."

00:04:09.901 --> 00:04:11.834
-Yeah, a little film.
-Little film.

00:04:11.834 --> 00:04:13.033
-No big deal.

00:04:13.033 --> 00:04:15.300
-So, he directed this,
and it's really sweet.

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:16.901
It's seen through
the eyes of Ruby the Roo,

00:04:16.901 --> 00:04:18.567
who I voice this character.

00:04:18.567 --> 00:04:21.601
She's gift-shop kangaroo
and she's desperate

00:04:21.601 --> 00:04:24.667
to break out of the gift shop
and explore the country.

00:04:24.667 --> 00:04:26.467
And she's very innocent
and curious and warm

00:04:26.467 --> 00:04:29.133
and fun and lovely,
like Australians are, you know.

00:04:29.133 --> 00:04:31.300
-Yeah, they are. You're right.

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:34.033
I want to show everyone
a clip here.

00:04:34.033 --> 00:04:35.934
You can check out
the full film at australia.com,

00:04:35.934 --> 00:04:37.067
but here's a little clip.

00:04:37.067 --> 00:04:38.968
Here's Rose Byrne as Ruby
in "G'day."

00:04:38.968 --> 00:04:40.133
Take a look.

00:04:41.767 --> 00:04:42.934
-There are like thousands of

00:04:42.934 --> 00:04:44.067
things you can see
on the reef --

00:04:44.067 --> 00:04:45.634
coral, turtles,
boobies, tiny sea --

00:04:45.634 --> 00:04:49.367
-Wait a second.
Did you say "coral"?

00:04:49.367 --> 00:04:51.467
-G'day. Welcome aboard.

00:04:51.467 --> 00:04:54.067
-Whoo-hoo! Boat trip!
Come on, Louie!

00:04:54.067 --> 00:04:56.200
-This is humiliating.

00:04:56.200 --> 00:04:58.567
And also strangely comforting.

00:04:58.567 --> 00:05:00.534
-Hold on. Ooh! Ooh!

00:05:00.534 --> 00:05:02.033
Excuse me.
-Let's go, folks.

00:05:02.033 --> 00:05:03.400
-What are you doing?
We're not going to make it!

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:05.267
-Yes, we are!
-Ohhhh!

00:05:05.267 --> 00:05:08.033
-Whoo-hoo!

00:05:08.033 --> 00:05:09.734
-I mean, come on.

00:05:09.734 --> 00:05:11.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:11.067 --> 00:05:13.200
"G'day." Rose Byrne.

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:15.901
We are playing a fun game with
Rose after the break.

00:05:15.901 --> 00:05:17.367
Stay here for more
from your short film

00:05:17.367 --> 00:05:18.467
from Tourism Australia.

00:05:18.467 --> 00:05:19.567
Stick around.

00:05:20.367 --> 00:05:22.133
-What a beautiful day
to go snorkeling.

00:05:22.133 --> 00:05:24.067
You guys been out to the
Great Barrier Reef before?

00:05:24.067 --> 00:05:26.467
-[ Gasps ]
The Great Barrier Reef!

00:05:26.467 --> 00:05:27.501
Huh?

00:05:27.501 --> 00:05:29.200
-Here we are!
-[ Gasps ]

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:30.234
G'day.

00:05:30.234 --> 00:05:31.868
-Uh, where am I?

00:05:31.868 --> 00:05:33.167
-Australia.

00:05:33.167 --> 00:05:34.667
And you look like
you need a vacation.

00:05:34.667 --> 00:05:37.133
-Show us what you got.
-Let's go.

00:05:37.133 --> 00:05:39.300
-Welcome to
the Sydney Opera House.

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:40.767
-It's remarkable.

00:05:40.767 --> 00:05:42.601
-Yep. it's amazing.

00:05:42.601 --> 00:05:43.634
Whoa!

00:05:43.634 --> 00:05:45.634
-I love it! What is it?

00:05:45.634 --> 00:05:47.667
-A wombat.
-♪ Australia ♪

00:05:47.667 --> 00:05:48.767
-Oh!

00:05:48.767 --> 00:05:50.067
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:50.067 --> 00:05:52.300
-I see kangaroos.
-Me too.

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:53.801
-Come on!

00:05:54.934 --> 00:05:55.934
-G'day, mate.

00:05:55.934 --> 00:05:57.501
-Hear that? We're mates.

00:05:57.501 --> 00:05:58.601
Aaaah!

00:05:58.601 --> 00:05:59.801
-Whoo-hoo!

00:05:59.801 --> 00:06:01.267
-Aaaaah!

00:06:01.267 --> 00:06:02.667
-Jump!

00:06:02.667 --> 00:06:04.067
-♪ I come from
a land down under ♪

00:06:04.067 --> 00:06:05.667
-G'day. My name is Freddie.

00:06:05.667 --> 00:06:07.934
-Wow! There's nothing
like Australia.

00:06:07.934 --> 00:06:10.467
-Special, huh?
-It would make a great movie.

00:06:10.467 --> 00:06:11.868
-[ Gasps ]

00:06:11.868 --> 00:06:14.400
-So, what are you waiting for?
Come and say g'day.

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:16.267
-♪ Whoa, oh, oh ♪

00:06:16.267 --> 00:06:19.467
♪ We come from
a land down under ♪

